      "title": "Forbes Lab - UCSD",
      "headings": [],
      "text": "Forbes Lab Structure and Function of the Eukaryotic Nucleus Research Projects Publications and Vitae Members Photos Map of UCSD Division of Biological Sciences Links The focus of our research is the eukaryotic nucleus: its structure and function. A primary area of interest is the nuclear pore, a large macromolecular envelope. All communication between the nucleus and cytoplasm occurs through the nuclear pore: the pore actively imports proteins needed for DNA replication, RNA transcription;and gene control, while excluding cytoplasmic proteins. The pore also must export messenger RNA, tRNA, snRNAs, and ribosomal precursors. With respect to the nuclear pore, we are studying: (1) the mechanism of nuclear transport, (2) the structure and component proteins of the pore, and (3) reconstitution of the nuclear pore in vitro. University of California, San Diego Section of Cell and Developmental Biology Division of Biological Sciences 9500 Gilman Drive Pacific Hall, Room 2128 La Jolla, CA 92093-0347 lab: (858) 534-6346 fax: (858) 534-0555",
